      "synonyms": [],
      "curator_alias": "",
      "note": "Minor coat protein pIII is located at the tail of the filamentous phage particle. It is involved in termination of assembly and infectivity. In the absence of pIII abnormally long phage particles are formed and remain attached to host cells. In addition, pIII is involved in initiating infection of host cells by binding to pili. In the case of the Ff phages, pIII binds to the tip of F-pili and then interacts with the TolA protein. The assembly termination function maps to the C-terminus of pIII, whereas the receptor binding maps to the N-terminus. Ike and f1 proteins cannot replace one another. Functions: receptor binding, morphogenesis, structural.",
